>>
>> I have to inform that I reuploaded the wiki. Now most of the hyperlinks
>> for pages starting with "Old Pages: " are fixed.
>
>
> Can=92t we get rid of the "Old Pages:" prefix anyway? It doesn=92t seem t=
o
> make a lot of sense =85 in a wiki. Whether a page was on the TikiWiki bef=
ore
> or not doesn=92t tell about its relevance.
>


There were any complaints that Tiki was old, old-fashioned, not coherent,
containing a lot of pages with discussions that newbies couldn't
understand. This for sure has diverted and continues to divert a lot of
people from Lojban. I can see that now from Google Analytics plugin
although it has been working just for several days (we have ~30 unique
visits a day to lojban.org).

This is why LMW was born. *All pages from the old wiki are not official or
worth reading by default by newbies.* But if you feel that any page is
still relevant, please fix links there, fix formatting, check whether
hyperlinks there lead only to good pages as well and at last rename that
page removing "Old Pages: " prefix but retaining redirect.


